        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Figure 1: The coskewness objective in isolation. (a) First X-weight vector (absolute value, unit norm) on the planted-skew design (7): the covariance objective loads on the linear decoy  $ x_{2} $, while the coskewness and combined objectives recover the planted direction  $ z^{*} $. (b) Basin transition of the combined objective on a companion design with a competing covariance-attractive direction: as the coskewness weight  $ \\gamma $ grows, the recovered direction switches sharply from the linear to the skewed axis.</div>\n",
